// TEST: a generic row's sum beside a Float64, forwarded by a caret caller, at a complex row (rejects)
// ERROR: BL3019 @ 14:15
// ============================================================================
// casts/545 through one more generic function: `outer(q: T^1)` only forwards
// its row to `halfsum`, whose body shaped its own `row` (the reduce) and so
// filed the element obligation under the row's ELEMENT variable, while
// `outer`'s `q` is still its arity-1 variable. The obligation was not
// carried to `outer`, so `outer` over a complex row reached g++ (BL9002).
// It is now outer's, judged against the element its call gives `q`, and
// refused at that argument as `halfsum(zs)` is. A real row still computes.
// ============================================================================
function halfsum(row: T^1) = reduce(row, (+)) / Float64(2.0)
function outer(q: T^1) = halfsum(q)
let ok = outer(Float64([1.0, 3.0]))
let z = outer([Complex128(complex(1.0, 2.0)), Complex128(complex(3.0, 4.0))])
